<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's cenbank to cut reserve interest rate.</title>
<headline>Hungary's cenbank to cut reserve interest rate.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Wednesday it would cut the forint interest rate it pays on commercial banks' obligatory hard currency reserves to an annual 16 percent from the current 17 percent.</p>
<p>The cut goes into effect on February 16, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;The reduction of the...interest rates was prompted by the fact that the NBH wants to gradually unify the interest rates it pays on hard currency and forint deposits,&quot; the NBH said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
